Name: uBlock Origin
Short Name: uBlock0
URL: https://github.com/gorhill/uBlock
Version: 1.77.4
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: GPL-3.0
License File: LICENSE
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes

Description:
uBlock Origin is AI Browser's built-in ad and tracker blocker. It ships as
a Manifest V2 component extension that users can't remove; its toolbar
button is always pinned.

src/ (not checked in) is the unmodified uBlock0_1.77.4.chromium.zip release,
fetched and checksum-verified by //aib/scripts/fetch_ublock.py, which is
where the version and SHA-256 are pinned. The release's own LICENSE.txt is
copied here as LICENSE. The corresponding source is the 1.77.4 tag of
https://github.com/gorhill/uBlock.

Local Modifications:
- None to uBlock Origin's code. Packaging only:
  - _locales/ is trimmed to the UI locales AI Browser ships.
  - Peter Lowe's packaged list (assets/thirdparties/pgl.yoyo.org) isn't
    redistributed; uBlock Origin downloads it at its first list update.
  - The packaged filter lists and the manifest are served from a .pak
    (aib_ublock_resources.grd) instead of from the extension directory.
  - ComponentLoader adds AI Browser's public "key" (fixing the extension ID
    to mfhbhkgdijnaendiokmdbdedghofepdf) and a description to the manifest
    at load time.

Bundled filter lists keep their own licenses: uBlock Origin filters and
EasyList/EasyPrivacy (GPL-3.0, uAssets), the Public Suffix List (MPL-2.0) and
the Online Malicious URL Blocklist (CC0-1.0/MIT). The extension's lib/
directory carries its third-party libraries' own notices.
